        <body>
            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0141" n="109" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v11/pg109"/>

                <head>68. Memorandum of a Telephone Conversation Between the Secretary of State and
                    the Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff (Twining), Washington, June 11, 1958,
                    8:59 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d68-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1958-06-11T08:59:00-04:00"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">June 11, 1958, 8:59
                    a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">TELEPHONE CALL TO GENERAL TWINING</p>
                <p>The Sec said the Pres, the PM and he had quite a talk at the WH re Lebanon. The
                    Sec thought T should know it is tensing up quite considerably there and we sent
                    a message to Chamoun on behalf of the Pres and PM which reaffirms assurances
                        given.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d68-f2"/> T wondered about extra measures—they
                    are on a 48-hour basis. The Pres, said the Sec, said to raise with T whether it
                    should be a 24-hour basis. T will look into it this a.m. It looks as though the
                    Soviets will veto the res in the SC,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d68-f3"/> said the
                    Sec, and that may bring things to a head. We may follow up by calling in the
                    GA.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
